==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|LL-Q150 (fra)-Lyokoï-partir en fumée.wav|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{lb|fr|intransitive|simultaneously|_|euphemistic|_|and, usually|hyperbolic}} to be consumed by and destroyed in fire (which is only implied) such that smoke is the only evidence of something having happened (ash, smut, etc. notwithstanding)
#: {{syn|fr|[[réduire en cendres|être réduit en cendres]]}}
# {{lb|fr|intransitive|figuratively}} to be [[ruined]], [[destroyed]]
#: {{syn|fr|[[s'en aller]] [[en ruine]]}}
# {{lb|fr|intransitive|figuratively}} to [[go up in smoke]], [[vanish into thin air]]

====Usage notes====
* As one may make substitutions for either of the phrase's two primary elements (the verbal {{m|fr|partir}} and its complementary {{m|fr|en [[fumée]]}}), a number of alternative phrasings, representing different levels of formality and used with varying levels of frequency, are possible: 
** with any number of substitutions for {{m|fr|partir}}, the most common including<ref name="tlfi-fumée">{{R:TLFi|fumée}}</ref> {{m|fr|s'en aller}}, {{l|fr|s'évanouir}} and {{m|fr|disparaître}}:
*** {{m|fr|s'en aller en fumée}} <ref name="tlfi-aller">{{R:TLFi|aller}}</ref><ref name="larousse-fumée">{{R:Larousse|fumée}}</ref> 
*** {{m|fr|s'évanouir en fumée}} <ref name="larousse-fumée" />
** and with {{m|fr|[[comme]] [[une]] [[fumée]]}}, {{m|fr||comme fumée}} <ref name="tlfi-fumée" />, or {{m|fr||comme en fumée}} for {{m|fr||en fumée}}:
*** {{m|fr||partir comme en fumée}}
*** {{m|fr||s'évanouir comme en fumée}}
*** {{m|fr||disparaître comme en fumée}}, {{m|fr||disparaître comme une fumée}}

